From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:39:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wolfSSL: fix peer-fingerprint certificate verification

wolfSSL passes an X509_STORE_CTX without OpenVPN's verify_callback
to cert_verify_callback. The nested X509_verify_cert() can therefore
reject fingerprint-only peers despite the fingerprint check succeeding.

Explicitly install verify_callback on the store context for wolfSSL
builds so nested verification follows OpenVPN's existing CA and
fingerprint verification policy.
---
 src/openvpn/ssl_openssl.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/src/openvpn/ssl_openssl.c
+++ b/src/openvpn/ssl_openssl.c
@@ -319,6 +319,11 @@ cert_verify_callback(X509_STORE_CTX *ctx
 
     /* Configure CRLs. */
     X509_STORE_CTX_set0_crls(ctx, session->opt->ssl_ctx->crls);
+
+#ifdef ENABLE_CRYPTO_WOLFSSL
+    X509_STORE_CTX_set_verify_cb(ctx, verify_callback);
+#endif
+
     return X509_verify_cert(ctx);
 }
 
